WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.234
-You look fantastic.
-I do.

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:04.300
-I love this, I love the jacket.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.267
You really do.
You know, I haven't seen you --

00:00:06.267 --> 00:00:09.167
-You accept compliments
in America -- yes.

00:00:09.167 --> 00:00:10.567
-Oh, you just agree to it.
-You agree.

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:12.901
-You go, "Yeah."
How's our pal Rita Ora?

00:00:12.901 --> 00:00:14.734
How's Rita doing?
-She's good.

00:00:14.734 --> 00:00:16.701
-She's no longer my pal.
She's my wife now.

00:00:16.701 --> 00:00:18.801
-[ Laughing ] Congratulations.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.801 --> 00:00:21.334
I didn't get the invitation.
I didn't get the invitation

00:00:21.334 --> 00:00:22.467
'cause I didn't know.
-No one did.

00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:24.534
No one was invited.
-Yeah.

00:00:24.534 --> 00:00:26.133
-No, no.
-She's one of my favorites.

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:27.534
And you two together
are just unbelievable.

00:00:27.534 --> 00:00:29.734
-Yeah.
-I know that she surprised you

00:00:29.734 --> 00:00:32.634
with this trip to Scotland.

00:00:32.634 --> 00:00:35.300
-Yeah, it wasn't one of those --
a surprise, "Hey!"

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:40.367
an all, massive, big,
giant extravaganza in Scotland.

00:00:40.367 --> 00:00:41.801
It was really just her

00:00:41.801 --> 00:00:46.601
wanting to go to this
one specific place.

00:00:46.601 --> 00:00:49.834
So Airbnb have these, like,
pop-up experiences you can do,

00:00:49.834 --> 00:00:52.734
and they did the Barbie house,
obviously, for the movie.

00:00:52.734 --> 00:00:57.601
But Rita found an article online
where they'd re-created

00:00:57.601 --> 00:01:01.400
a replica of Shrek's house.
-Uh-huh, yeah, yeah.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.968
-In Scotland.
And it was just --

00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:05.234
And it was open
to anyone to go and stay.

00:01:05.234 --> 00:01:08.634
And she said, "I think
we're gonna go do that,"

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:12.000
and made me go to Scotland

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.734
just to stay it's Shrek's house.
-Yeah.

00:01:14.734 --> 00:01:17.133
So she showed you this on...?

00:01:17.133 --> 00:01:18.734
-Yeah, and I said, "Ha ha.
That's funny,"

00:01:18.734 --> 00:01:20.467
and she said,
"I'll tell you what's funny.

00:01:20.467 --> 00:01:21.667
We're going."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:25.367
And then dragged me to --
Didn't drag me.

00:01:25.367 --> 00:01:27.300
I was into it.
Took me to Scotland.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:28.868
And then we got there,
and you had to drive

00:01:28.868 --> 00:01:31.834
like 40 minutes off
the main road, over dirt roads,

00:01:31.834 --> 00:01:33.033
and it's, like,
in the middle of nowhere.

00:01:33.033 --> 00:01:34.167
It felt like a trick.

00:01:34.167 --> 00:01:36.167
Felt like,
"Did I do something wrong?

00:01:36.167 --> 00:01:38.567
Is this the last time
I'm going to see anyone?"

00:01:38.567 --> 00:01:40.367
-Life.
-The last -- is this it?

00:01:40.367 --> 00:01:41.501
-The sunshine.
Yeah, this is over.

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:43.334
Yeah, of course.
-And then we got out there,

00:01:43.334 --> 00:01:44.534
and it's beautiful.

00:01:44.534 --> 00:01:46.367
Like, just so much effort,

00:01:46.367 --> 00:01:48.067
and right down
to the finest detail.

00:01:48.067 --> 00:01:51.801
Inside was -- looked
exactly like in the movie.

00:01:51.801 --> 00:01:56.000
Then she says, "Put that on,"
and made me dress up as Shrek.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:57.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.968 --> 00:01:59.334
And she pulled out --

00:01:59.334 --> 00:02:01.367
And everyone -- there's
some, like, videos and photos,

00:02:01.367 --> 00:02:04.834
and everyone thinks we took
a camera crew with us.

00:02:04.834 --> 00:02:08.801
It was just us two, and she put
green paint all over herself.

00:02:08.801 --> 00:02:10.667
-Now, do you --
Am I missing something?

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:12.767
Do you like Shrek?

00:02:12.767 --> 00:02:15.033
-Not that much. I mean...
-Yeah, okay.

00:02:15.033 --> 00:02:17.167
Does she like Shrek that much?
Just out of...

00:02:17.167 --> 00:02:18.934
-Clearly.
-Yeah.

00:02:18.934 --> 00:02:20.534
-I didn't know about that.
I didn't know about

00:02:20.534 --> 00:02:22.067
this infatuation.

00:02:22.067 --> 00:02:25.734
-Well, here's -- here's --
here's Rita as Fiona.

00:02:25.734 --> 00:02:28.234
But I want to show you.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.234 --> 00:02:30.400
Let me zoom in.
Here's you as Shrek.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.334
-There's me.
[ Laughs ]

00:02:32.334 --> 00:02:34.634
Look at that.
-It's unbelievable.

00:02:34.634 --> 00:02:36.968
-Look at that mask.
-Unbelievable.

00:02:36.968 --> 00:02:39.400
You know, I know you as a --
as a fun human being.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:41.467
You're always nice to me.

00:02:41.467 --> 00:02:44.634
But you're very talented,
and I respect your work.

00:02:44.634 --> 00:02:46.067
-That's also true.
-Yeah.

00:02:46.067 --> 00:02:48.467
-And, also --
but I love your fashion.

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:50.467
And I think you're a
good-looking dude

00:02:50.467 --> 00:02:53.400
and a stylish dude.
And I go, "Well, here we go."

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:54.934
I get this thing to go --
did you see? --

00:02:54.934 --> 00:02:56.934
the Hermès fashion show?
-Yeah.

00:02:56.934 --> 00:02:58.968
I don't know.
Just the things I do

00:02:58.968 --> 00:03:00.868
when I get bored is walk
for Hermès

00:03:00.868 --> 00:03:04.000
in New York Fashion Week.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:06.400
I don't know
how I got in that door.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:08.801
-They go, "Have you seen Taika?
Have you seen Taika's,

00:03:08.801 --> 00:03:10.167
what he's doing?"
And I go, "What?"

00:03:10.167 --> 00:03:13.033
So they -- Hermès had you
walking the runway

00:03:13.033 --> 00:03:15.000
in their fashion --
at New York Fashion Week.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.200
For real.
-It's been quite the year, guys.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:20.467
-Look at you.

00:03:20.467 --> 00:03:23.534
Now, see...

00:03:23.534 --> 00:03:25.133
Is that face...
-Are you upset?

00:03:25.133 --> 00:03:27.000
-...too intense?
-Yeah.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:29.667
You got really --
-Is it selling the jackets,

00:03:29.667 --> 00:03:31.868
or is it just saying,
"Get out of my way"?

00:03:31.868 --> 00:03:33.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.133 --> 00:03:35.434
-I mean, it's -- it's not --
-It's not that.

00:03:35.434 --> 00:03:37.601
-It's not this guy.
I mean...

00:03:37.601 --> 00:03:38.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.667 --> 00:03:40.400
-That's the same guy.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:41.968
-It's the same coat.
-Same person.

00:03:41.968 --> 00:03:43.300
-It's the same outfit.
-Same outfit.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:46.634
-It's the same coat.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.634 --> 00:03:48.534
It's the same coat, but it's
just worn different ways.

00:03:48.534 --> 00:03:50.267
-It's just attitude.
That's why I wear Hermès.

00:03:50.267 --> 00:03:52.100
-It's attitude.
-It's attitude.

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:55.000
-This is actually the same suit.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.701
-We split it up.
-My attitude's different.

00:03:56.701 --> 00:03:58.033
-Yeah. Your attitude changes
a little bit, yeah.

00:03:58.033 --> 00:03:59.834
-It really looks like this.
-Yeah. I think you have

00:03:59.834 --> 00:04:02.501
a very positive attitude.

00:04:02.501 --> 00:04:05.801
-I think I'm probably a very --
I'm probably the perfect model

00:04:05.801 --> 00:04:08.033
'cause the only thing
I cared about was

00:04:08.033 --> 00:04:09.934
if the clothes looked good.

00:04:09.934 --> 00:04:12.067
And if that small
little company,

00:04:12.067 --> 00:04:13.767
Hermès, would sell
some of these jackets.

00:04:13.767 --> 00:04:15.467
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.467 --> 00:04:17.667
-Small little company.
Yeah.

00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:19.868
Can we talk about your film,
"Next Goal Wins"?

00:04:19.868 --> 00:04:21.567
-Yes, please.
-This is --

00:04:21.567 --> 00:04:23.734
It's in theaters this Friday.
"Next Goal Wins."

00:04:23.734 --> 00:04:26.567
It's based on a true story.
How'd you hear about the story?

00:04:26.567 --> 00:04:29.200
-So, a few years ago,
there was a documentary made.

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:33.000
And it's a true story of the
worst soccer team in the world.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:36.167
So --
And that's American Samoa.

00:04:36.167 --> 00:04:37.667
They're no longer the worst.

00:04:37.667 --> 00:04:39.567
It's not really a spoiler,
but --

00:04:39.567 --> 00:04:41.434
But back then --
In the history of the country,

00:04:41.434 --> 00:04:44.701
they'd never won a game
or scored a goal.

00:04:44.701 --> 00:04:46.400
And they still hold the record
for the biggest

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:48.701
international loss,

00:04:48.701 --> 00:04:51.767
and that's against Australia,
and they lost 31-0.

00:04:51.767 --> 00:04:53.667
-Oh, stop.
-Yeah.

00:04:53.667 --> 00:04:55.901
-Can't they call it
after a certain amount of goals?

00:04:55.901 --> 00:04:57.167
-You can't -- I don't know.

00:04:57.167 --> 00:04:58.534
They're throwing all the towels
onto the field.

00:04:58.534 --> 00:05:01.801
So, no, they -- and after that,
you'd think they would --

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:04.701
that would deter most people
from playing again,

00:05:04.701 --> 00:05:07.067
but they had the tenacity and
the determination to get better.

00:05:07.067 --> 00:05:09.734
And they got a coach in, who's
played by Michael Fassbender,

00:05:09.734 --> 00:05:11.200
and he turns the team around.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:12.834
And he's a bit of a lost soul,
as well,

00:05:12.834 --> 00:05:14.934
so they turn him around,
and they --

00:05:14.934 --> 00:05:16.634
and together they kind of
create, like a really nice,

00:05:16.634 --> 00:05:18.734
sort of happy family together,

00:05:18.734 --> 00:05:23.400
and they go on to --
to play a game...

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:24.667
-Yeah.
-...of soccer.

00:05:24.667 --> 00:05:26.100
-Yeah. Okay.
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:27.901
You're not giving any spoilers.
-Not giving anything.

00:05:27.901 --> 00:05:31.000
-No! Don't give anything away.
It's a great film.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:32.467
-Here's a great idea.
Make a film

00:05:32.467 --> 00:05:35.434
about the worst soccer team
in the world who get even worse

00:05:35.434 --> 00:05:36.968
by the end.
-Yeah, they lose.

00:05:36.968 --> 00:05:38.100
-Everyone wants to see that.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:39.934
-Yeah, they lose at the end.
Yeah.

00:05:39.934 --> 00:05:42.300
The whole cast is great, though.
Mike Fassbender is great.

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:45.133
Everybody in the film is great.
And there's this kid.

00:05:45.133 --> 00:05:46.901
Can you tell me about Armani?
-Oh, yeah.

00:05:46.901 --> 00:05:48.901
There's a kid
in the film called Armani.

00:05:48.901 --> 00:05:51.367
So when I approached this film,
I just wanted to be very open

00:05:51.367 --> 00:05:54.033
and fluid to this,
the creative process.

00:05:54.033 --> 00:05:56.567
You know, any idea's
worth trying.

00:05:56.567 --> 00:05:58.901
And not to be so rigid
in my in my approach.

00:05:58.901 --> 00:06:00.267
And as a result,

00:06:00.267 --> 00:06:02.701
I was sort of just open
to whatever was going on.

00:06:02.701 --> 00:06:04.968
And Michael came over
after about a week and a half

00:06:04.968 --> 00:06:09.267
of shooting, and he said,
"Man, I've just met this --

00:06:09.267 --> 00:06:11.834
some 10- or 11-year-old kid
over by the unit table,

00:06:11.834 --> 00:06:14.133
and I don't know who he is
or where he comes from,

00:06:14.133 --> 00:06:16.501
but he's fascinating.
I wish he was in the movie."

00:06:16.501 --> 00:06:18.534
And I said, "Well, let's just
put him in the movie."

00:06:18.534 --> 00:06:20.968
And so that kid just kept --
we just told the kid

00:06:20.968 --> 00:06:22.400
to keep turning up every day,

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:24.200
and he came in,
and he's a really big part

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:26.367
of the movie now.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:26.367 --> 00:06:27.801
-That's just great.
-That's just great.

00:06:27.801 --> 00:06:29.267
-And he's like,
you keep showing up...

00:06:29.267 --> 00:06:31.901
-Just go show -- go and be --
and go hang around movie sets.

00:06:31.901 --> 00:06:33.200
That's what everyone wants.

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:35.167
Really good advice --
go hang around movie sets.

00:06:35.167 --> 00:06:37.834
-Yeah, but that's the vibe.
You put love into the movie,

00:06:37.834 --> 00:06:39.200
and you get love
out of the movie.

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:40.400
-That's exactly right.
-What I'm talking about, buddy.

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:42.000
I want to show a clip.
Here's a look

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.701
